      <h2 class="noodle-band__slogan" id="band-title">Better noodles weren't for sale. <em>So we made them.</em></h2>
      <p class="noodle-band__body">
        The noodles are made in our own Noodle Room in Crown Point, and the broth is simmered there every morning and driven out before service.
      </p>
    </div>
    <a class="noodle-band__cta" href="/noodle-room/">
      See the Noodle Room
      <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M1 7H13M13 7L7.5 1.5M13 7L7.5 12.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round"/>
      </svg>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

{# ==================== NEAREST NEIGHBOUR ==================== #}
{#
  Brief: "Nearest neighbour link: /tajima-mercury/ only." Not all six. Linking
  every location from every location page is how six pages become one
  undifferentiated blob to a crawler.

  SUSHI CLAIM CORRECTED 2026-08-05. This read "the full bar and the only sushi
  in San Diego." Both halves of that were wrong.

  It was false inside Tajima: East Village's live Toast catalog carries a
  Salmon Sushi Hand Roll and a Spicy Tuna Sushi Hand Roll, both $6.50, filed
  under Appetizers (Open Decision #20, which corrected CLIENT_FACTS.md on
  2026-08-04; this page was missed). It also parsed as a claim against every
  restaurant in San Diego, which is not a claim we are in a position to make
  about anyone.

  CLIENT_FACTS.md sets the rule for this exact case: "What Mercury uniquely
  has is the full sushi programme ... Write scale, not exclusivity." So the
  line now states the size of Mercury's list, scoped to Tajima, and claims
  sole possession of nothing.

  Verified against the catalogs 2026-08-05: Mercury is the only San Diego room
  with a dedicated Sushi section (4 sashimi plates and 10 rolls, 14 items);
  East Village has 2 hand rolls under Appetizers; Convoy and College Heights
  carry poke but no sushi; Crown Point and Plaza Bonita have neither.

  Note "in the house" means across Tajima, the same scoping
  /tajima-college-heights/ uses for its tap list. Do not widen it to San Diego.
#}
<section class="sect" aria-labelledby="near-title">
  <div class="sect__inner">
    <header class="sect__head">
      <span class="sect__eyebrow">Nearby</span>
      <h2 class="sect__title" id="near-title">Two miles up the road.</h2>
      <p class="sect__note">
        <a class="sect__link" href="/tajima-mercury/">Tajima Ramen Mercury</a> is the bigger room. Around ninety seats, a full bar with Japanese whisky, and the widest sushi list in the house. Or see <a class="sect__link" href="/locations/">all six San Diego rooms</a>.
      </p>
    </header>
  </div>
</section>
